==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~40 seconds<sup>300f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Duche]]s spawn, delay 10~40 seconds<sup>300f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[R.Ost]] spawns as the boss.
**30 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.13 seconds<sup>2f~4f</sup>.
**20 [[Duche]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.33 seconds<sup>2f~10f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage introduces a great threat later on, R.Ost, which is a heavy pusher with high health, damage, and attack speed. In this stage, you can use area attackers such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris/Cyborg Cat]] or [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] to deal gradual damage, while deploying stallers. You can also use [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] along with these cats to speed up the process. Alternatively, you can use stackable attackers such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon/Dragon Cat]] to help deal damage.

In higher crowns, you can use [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]] to deal very high damage to all peons in this stage and manage the R.Ost's pushing power, since Jagando's knockback ability is able to keep him at bay.

